; Trusted call-effects summaries of the Path B runtime helpers in be/nfcxx_ldrt.c (long double, __int128 and
; _Float128 arithmetic, comparisons and conversions), for scripts/pathb-borrowck.rb --effects. Every value is a
; 16-byte object: a helper writes all 16 bytes of its first pointer argument (init) and reads its const pointer
; arguments (read). Helpers touching other memory (bit-fields, va_list, the ubsan report) are not described.
; The checked conversions abort on a value that does not fit, which is not a return. Regenerate after changing the
; helpers' signatures, and check each new writer stores all 16 bytes.
